<article class="env-lemma" id="0CBB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CBB">Lemma <span data-tag="0CBB">100.8.6</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{X}' \to \mathcal{Y}$ be morphisms of algebraic stacks. If $\mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{X}'$ is a monomorphism then the canonical diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathcal{X} \ar[r] \ar[d] &  \mathcal{X} \times _\mathcal {Y} \mathcal{X} \ar[d] \\  \mathcal{X}' \ar[r] &  \mathcal{X}' \times _\mathcal {Y} \mathcal{X}' }  \]
</div>
  <p> is a fibre product square. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We have $\mathcal{X} = \mathcal{X} \times _{\mathcal{X}'} \mathcal{X}$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/04ZZ" data-tag="04ZZ">100.8.4</a>. Thus the result by applying Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/04Z1" data-tag="04Z1">4.31.13</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>